cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the papers it implements."
title: "heterogeneous-front-tracking: front tracking for u_t + (g(x)|u|^p)_x = 0"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Venkatesh"
    given-names: "Parasuram"
    affiliation: "TIFR Centre for Applicable Mathematics, Bengaluru"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-2681-1982"
repository-code: "https://github.com/parasuramv/heterogeneous-front-tracking"
abstract: >-
  Front tracking for the heterogeneous scalar conservation law
  u_t + (g(x)|u|^p)_x = 0, p > 1, on the line or the circle, with g
  approximated by its piecewise-affine nodal interpolant. Fronts are
  closed-form curves, event times solve linear equations, and transverse
  zeros of a sign-changing g act as absorbing interfaces. Convergence as
  the discretisation is refined is studied empirically only.
keywords:
  - conservation laws
  - front tracking
  - spatially heterogeneous flux
  - entropy solutions
  - numerical analysis
